  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Eastern Shore&#8217;s construction overhead contains payroll charges for administrative personal who indirectly allocate portions of their time to construction projects as a whole. The dollars associated with the allocation are spread evenly across all construction projects that take place each month. Construction projects are typically projects with a higher use of labor which includes Mains, Compressor Stations, and Meter/Regulator Stations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
